.TH pvc-fn-response 1  "pvc-fn-response " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-fn\-response \- Synthesize a `.fr` frequency\-response file from a breakpoint or partial table, rather than analyzing a sound file (`pvc freqresponse` does that instead)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-fn\-response\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Synthesize a `.fr` frequency\-response file from a breakpoint or partial table, rather than analyzing a sound file (`pvc freqresponse` does that instead)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pvc\-fn\-response\-filtresponsemaker(1)
Ports `filtresponsemaker` (`legacy/pvc_src/filtresponsemaker.c`): a "frequency gradient" response, linearly interpolated in dB between unordered `(frequency\-or\-octave.pitchclass, decibels)` breakpoints
.TP
pvc\-fn\-response\-chordresponsemaker(1)
Ports `chordresponsemaker` (`legacy/pvc_src/ chordresponsemaker.c`): a stack of harmonic\-partial tones, each with a triangular\- or rectangular\-windowed dB rolloff around its center frequency, from unordered sextuples `(pitch\-or\-Hz, num_partials, bandwidth, decibels, partial_spacing, db_rolloff_per_octave)`
.TP
pvc\-fn\-response\-groupdelaymaker(1)
Ports `groupdelaymaker` (`legacy/pvc_src/groupdelaymaker.c`): like `chordresponsemaker`, but each bin\*(Aqs response is an `(amp, delay\-time)` pair instead of `(amp, frequency)`, from unordered septuples `(pitch\-or\-Hz, num_partials, bandwidth, decibels, partial_spacing, db_rolloff_total, delay_secs)`. See `pvc\-core:: tools::groupdelaymaker`\*(Aqs doc comment for the real differences from `chordresponsemaker`\*(Aqs own dB\-rolloff/edge\-falloff formulas
.TP
pvc\-fn\-response\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
